      "evidence_or_problem": "Source: [00:05:01\u201300:05:31] - 'in the opposite case, when x and y are dependent, then the observation of y somehow changes the distribution of x.'"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For independent random variables, joint distribution factors as P(X) * P(Y)",
      "supported": true,
      "evidence_or_problem": "Source: [00:04:13\u201300:05:01] - 'independence means that the joint distribution P of x, y can be decomposed as a product. P of x times P of y.'"
